// Draconic Tail (combat log line on each strike)
@26 = ~Draconic Tail~

// Acid Breath
@30 = ~Acid Breath~
@31 = ~Acid Breath

The Black Dragon Disciple exhales a 15-ft. long, 5-ft. wide line of acid, dealing 4d4 acid damage to all creatures in the line (save vs. Breath for half). The damage increases to 6d4 at level 7, 8d4 at level 11, 10d4 at level 17 and 12d4 at level 19, when the line also grows to 30 ft. long and 10 ft. wide. Allies in the line are affected.

Usable once per day, twice at level 7, three times at level 11 and four times at level 17.~

// Frightful Presence
@40 = ~Frightful Presence~
@41 = ~Frightful Presence

The Black Dragon Disciple radiates an aura of draconic menace. Enemies of a lower level than the Black Dragon Disciple within 15 ft. must save vs. Spell or be panicked for 2 rounds. Whether it succeeds or fails, a creature then becomes immune to this aura for 24 hours. Allies are not affected.

Using this ability turns the aura on; it can then be dismissed at will.~
@42 = ~Dismiss Frightful Presence~
@43 = ~Dismiss Frightful Presence

Turns off the Frightful Presence aura. It can be turned on again at will.~

// Draconic Wings (helmet slot item, and the innate abilities that spread / fold them)
@60 = ~Draconic Wings~
@61 = ~Draconic Wings

Leathery wings have torn free from the back of the Black Dragon Disciple. They take the place of a helmet.

STATISTICS:

Movement: +4
Immunity to critical hits~
@62 = ~Draconic Wings

The Black Dragon Disciple spreads his draconic wings, gaining +4 movement speed and immunity to critical hits. The wings occupy the helmet slot.

Using this ability spreads the wings; they can then be folded at will.~
@63 = ~Fold Draconic Wings~
@64 = ~Fold Draconic Wings

The Black Dragon Disciple folds his wings and frees the helmet slot. They can be spread again at will.~

// Fight with / without the Bite (innate abilities that swap themselves)
@70 = ~Fight with the Bite~
@71 = ~Fight with the Bite

The Black Dragon Disciple bares his fangs: the bite takes the off hand again and gives one more attack per round, with the usual two-weapon penalties.

Using this ability summons the bite; it can then be dismissed at will.~
@72 = ~Fight without the Bite~
@73 = ~Fight without the Bite

The Black Dragon Disciple fights with his claws alone, which lets him benefit from Single Weapon Style. The bite can be summoned again at will.~
